type: thesis
title: "Reduction-preserving multi-channel identifiability: which Fisher ranks survive a stiff–sloppy reduction?"
authors:
  - family-names: Ogbonna
    given-names: Kelechi Emeka
    email: kelechiogbonna300@gmail.com
    alias: cloudynirvana
    website: "https://github.com/cloudynirvana"
abstract: >-
  After a documented stiff-sloppy or MBAM-style reduction, which multi-channel
  Fisher ranks from the full metabolic ODE survive on the reduced system, and
  which ranks are artefacts of the unreduced coordinates? On one synthetic
  eight-rate metabolic generator, a quasi-steady reduction that keeps the
  product kappa leaves the practical ranks of the shared schedules unchanged:
  the lactate/glucose ratio stays at 1, and the four-channel snapshot stays at
  5, so the multi-channel advantage of 4 survives. The schedule that records
  the deleted modifier has practical rank 6 and no reduced counterpart.
  Numerical eigenvalues in the deleted plane vanish and never cleared the
  practical cut. Not a medical device.
